<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 16:33:43 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Across Africa</category><title>Navi Pillay: Fighting violence with justice</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/navi-pillay-fighting-violence-with-justice</link><description>
From the International Criminal Court to Africa’s place in the global justice system, the stakes are high. In an exclusive interview, Nobel Peace Prize winner, Navi Pillay will discuss international justice . She says it it must not be held hostage to political power, as Donald Trump targets the ICC. What does this showdown mean for Africa?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/667b0550-d933-11f1-80f6-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8219ec1f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/667b0550-d933-11f1-80f6-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8219ec1f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">591b06f6-d92b-11f1-8c2e-8394b69f450d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 16:12:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Clarisse FORTUNÉ</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: 'Donald Trump's wings have been more than clipped'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-us-midterms-donald-trump-s-wings-have-been-more-than-clipped</link><description>
US President Donald Trump faced a radically transformed and hostile political landscape after Democrats seized both the House of Representatives and the Senate in Tuesday's (November 3) midterms. The result was a personal humiliation for the 80-year-old Trump, leaving him as a lame duck president for the remaining two years of his term. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/856c8c6e-d92d-11f1-bb12-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-616a321e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/856c8c6e-d92d-11f1-bb12-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-616a321e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">03fa6e1c-d92d-11f1-a24a-9d965d0685c4</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 15:46:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category><![CDATA[People & Profit]]></category><title>Global travel sector grows despite headwinds</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20261105-global-travel-sector-grows-despite-headwinds</link><description>
The global tourism sector is growing, despite conflicts and economic uncertainty. That's the finding of a new report by World Travel Market, which says the number of international arrivals is set to hit a record 1.57 billion in 2026. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b97cffc-d922-11f1-9e1e-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/Untitled-Sequence-01-27.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b97cffc-d922-11f1-9e1e-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/Untitled-Sequence-01-27.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1f5cf0e0-d922-11f1-9fd3-453fe506ab99</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 15:43:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Kate MOODY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Europe: Dozens of flights diverted following bomb threats</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-europe-dozens-of-flights-diverted-following-bomb-threats</link><description>
Hoax bomb threats hit at least 27 affected flights around Europe this week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/27b15c74-d92f-11f1-ba6f-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/Bomb-threats-EN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/27b15c74-d92f-11f1-ba6f-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/Bomb-threats-EN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e8d36bf2-d92c-11f1-86e8-3577fa92be1b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 15:40:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Identity crisis': Can Democrats 'deliver' following their 'historic', once in a generation victory?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/identity-crisis-can-democrats-deliver-following-their-historic-once-in-a-generation-victory</link><description>
A historic Democratic electoral breakthrough has transformed the American political landscape. For Laurie Dundon, Senior Associate Fellow at the European Leadership Network and former US diplomat, the central question is whether the Democratic Party can convert electoral momentum into coherent governance. "Can they deliver?" Dunden examines the apparent disintegration of Donald Trump's 2024 MAGA coalition alongside the Democratic Party's continuing ideological struggle between its progressive and centrist wings. Ahead of 2028, Dunden cautions against seeing Trump as a lame duck: "Trump is never going to stop being Trump." The resulting struggle over congressional spending powers, presidential vetoes, tariffs and investigations promises to be a delicate dance to watch".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa0c1d04-d924-11f1-b853-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-093517-094454-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa0c1d04-d924-11f1-b853-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-093517-094454-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ff4c7f5c-d924-11f1-9478-2bec2c80397b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 15:27:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel's main Arab list backs Eisenkot to form government after election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261105-israel-main-arab-list-backs-eisenkot-to-form-government-after-election</link><description>
Israel's largest Arab party grouping said Thursday it would recommend opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot to form the next government, potentially bolstering his bid after Arab-majority lists won a record 19 seats in last week's election and Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu lost the support of an allied religious party.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29eef780-d925-11f1-85c3-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4MA4Z2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29eef780-d925-11f1-85c3-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4MA4Z2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b73f77c2-d925-11f1-8916-039cf3b813a7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 14:43:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29eef780-d925-11f1-85c3-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4MA4Z2.jpg">© Jack Guez, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>Bringing the magic of Harry Potter to life through music</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261105-bringing-the-magic-of-harry-potter-to-life-through-music</link><description>
In this edition of Entre Nous, we meet Timothy Henty, the British conductor bringing the magic of Harry Potter to life in Paris. As part of the Harry Potter Film Concert Series, he leads more than 80 musicians in a spectacular live orchestral performance, offering audiences a unique opportunity to experience one of cinema's most beloved stories like never before.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30a94d50-d91b-11f1-bcce-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-WB-ENTRE-NOUS-HARRY-POTTER.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30a94d50-d91b-11f1-bcce-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-WB-ENTRE-NOUS-HARRY-POTTER.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">09d5d3cc-d91d-11f1-a1b9-fd32e701dbc4</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 14:30:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Delano D’SOUZA</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>British comedian Russell Brand found guilty of rape, sexual assault</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261105-british-comedian-russell-brand-found-guilty-of-rape-sexual-assault</link><description>
A London jury on Thursday convicted British comedian and actor Russell Brand of one count of rape and three counts of sexual assault. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53ca4e84-d924-11f1-a998-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6FC68G.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53ca4e84-d924-11f1-a998-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6FC68G.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8a15c7f2-d924-11f1-97ea-3127fc7c2620</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 14:26:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53ca4e84-d924-11f1-a998-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6FC68G.jpg">© Henry Nicholls, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France faces new protests as government seeks to prevent violence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france-faces-new-protests-as-government-seeks-to-prevent-violence</link><description>
France faces new protests as the government seeks to prevent a repeat of October unrest. Protesters demand better public services, including education, and also critique the rising cost-of-living. FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin reports from the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/98aad556-d923-11f1-8469-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-2ec8f03c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/98aad556-d923-11f1-8469-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-2ec8f03c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">99cad81a-d922-11f1-8cd4-4554a55e9742</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 14:19:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French bank hit by cyberattack, hackers steal $100 million</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/cyberattack-french-bank-says-online-hacking-stole-around-100-million</link><description>
French regional bank Crédit Mutuel Arkéa said Wednesday it had been hit by a cyberattack that led to fraudulent transfers worth around 100 million euros ($112 million). The bank said the attack, which has since been "contained", allowed hackers to access its own accounts and transfer funds to other banks. Customer accounts were not affected, and no losses were reported by clients.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b159f36-d922-11f1-a71c-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f04d7e6e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b159f36-d922-11f1-a71c-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f04d7e6e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">db3abdee-d920-11f1-a797-d10c6016a855</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 14:09:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>South African star Zolani Mahola: From 'Waka Waka' with Shakira to 'People Power'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261105-south-african-star-zolani-mahola-from-waka-waka-with-shakira-to-people-power</link><description>
From the global success of "Waka Waka" to her forthcoming second solo album "People Power", South Africa's Zolani Mahola has built a career around the power of music to bring people together.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/20ffb7de-d90e-11f1-8cbb-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c6f935c3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/20ffb7de-d90e-11f1-8cbb-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c6f935c3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">39361432-d90f-11f1-b2b4-85e7a8d368b9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 13:34:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Eve JACKSON</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>'It's fascinating to see a human becoming a person': Author Clémentine Goldszal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261105-it-s-fascinating-to-see-a-human-becoming-a-person-author-cl%C3%A9mentine-goldszal</link><description>
What is life like for a newly born, premature or sick baby? These are the questions tackled by a French journalist in her first ever book. Clémentine Goldszal asks what it means to be rushed from the delivery room to the neonatal intensive care unit, and what is means to enter the world before you are ready. Goldszal's book is entitled "Newborn: Inside the World of Neonatal Care". She spoke to us in Perspective.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1b758a4-d919-11f1-95f7-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-be40513f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1b758a4-d919-11f1-95f7-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-be40513f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a9171392-d8ff-11f1-8919-3f00dc60fa37</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 13:17:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Bent on leaving his mark: Trump's proposed 'Triumphal Arch' sparks backlash</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261105-bent-on-leaving-his-mark-trump-s-proposed-triumphal-arch-sparks-backlash</link><description>
Since his return to power, US President Donald Trump has been intent on reshaping the nation's capital Washington, seeking to leave his name and mark on it. After his involvement with the Kennedy Center, the White House ballroom and the Lincoln Memorial Reflecting Pool, Trump is now particularly keen on building a 250-foot (79-metre) "Triumphal Arch" – a project he claims is intended to honour the 250th anniversary of the United States.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0096512a-d86d-11f1-a062-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/V2-VI-FOCUS-FR-ARCHE-DE-TRUMP-FANNY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0096512a-d86d-11f1-a062-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/V2-VI-FOCUS-FR-ARCHE-DE-TRUMP-FANNY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c4c9c194-d86d-11f1-8342-57d0505eade3</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 12:55:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Fanny ALLARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>What comes next for Democrats after midterm election victory?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-what-comes-next-for-democrats-after-midterm-election-victory</link><description>
With the US midterms over, Democrats are turning to what could become one of their most crowded and unpredictable presidential primaries in decades – a 2028 contest ​likely to expose the party's divide over how to win back the White House. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/26e1fdac-d912-11f1-b02d-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4f347cf9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/26e1fdac-d912-11f1-b02d-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4f347cf9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">063a5ef8-d90f-11f1-8b1a-7ba2c54bd1c0</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 12:54:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Multiple flights in Europe diverted because of bomb threats after earlier hoaxes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-multiple-flights-in-europe-diverted-because-of-bomb-threats-after-earlier-hoaxes</link><description>
Multiple flights in Europe made emergency landings on Thursday after being diverted because of bomb threats. The incidents followed hoax bomb threats earlier this week that prompted searches, diversions and in one case a military escort.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8a87f438-d912-11f1-af4e-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261105-130140-130307-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8a87f438-d912-11f1-af4e-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261105-130140-130307-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8f8005de-d912-11f1-8b3d-954e8faaad66</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 12:52:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France: High schools blocked again as students reject government responses as 'meaningless'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-france-high-schools-blocked-again-as-students-reject-government-responses-as-meaningless</link><description>
🇫🇷 Students are blocking their schools and universities across France again this Thursday, November 5, despite the government’s response, which they deem insufficient.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5d5973ca-d916-11f1-999f-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/Manif-EN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5d5973ca-d916-11f1-999f-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/Manif-EN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ed538cf0-d915-11f1-96b7-fbefea7e8268</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 12:51:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Farewell Botox, heels and big hair: Is this the end of MAGA women?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261105-farewell-botox-heels-and-big-hair-is-this-the-end-of-maga-women</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, November 5: "Loser" and "Reborn in the USA" are just some of the headlines dominating the international press after the Democrats stomped to victory in the US midterm elections. What impact will their success have on the rest of Donald Trump's presidency? How will he govern with a Democratic-controlled Congress? These are just some of the burning questions after that vote. Also, do the midterm results signal the end of the MAGA woman and the "Mar-a-Lago face"?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ad6a6ec-d8e9-11f1-9fd5-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-11-05T06-25-45-514Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ad6a6ec-d8e9-11f1-9fd5-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-11-05T06-25-45-514Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0081c2e2-d8e9-11f1-a2db-4fa312074424</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 12:15:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dheepthika LAURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Bomb threats cause major flight disruptions across Europe</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-bomb-threats-cause-major-flight-disruptions-across-europe</link><description>
Bomb ​threats forced airliners to make unplanned landings across Europe on Thursday morning, the latest in a series of threats targeting flights in Europe. While no country has attributed blame for the threats, they come at a time ​when European officials have been blaming both Russia and Iran for what they describe as "hybrid attacks" and acts of sabotage. Moscow and Tehran both deny any such campaign. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b96c436c-d908-11f1-b45b-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261105-110119-110548-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b96c436c-d908-11f1-b45b-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261105-110119-110548-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">be068bbc-d908-11f1-ae95-8feabeb9851a</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 11:32:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: Elon Musk fails $440 million bet as Republicans lose</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-us-midterms-elon-musk-fails-440-million-bet-as-republicans-lose</link><description>
The 2026 midterm elections were the most expensive on record, with nearly 12 billion dollars spent during the campaign. Tech tycoon Elon Musk was by far the largest individual donor ever, injecting over 440 million dollars of his money to support the GOP. Tuesday's resounding Democratic victory showed the limits of his money, power and influence.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc745f1e-d907-11f1-9c91-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3b5ba1d6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc745f1e-d907-11f1-9c91-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3b5ba1d6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d7fd64a4-d904-11f1-8ebe-c1916dc679c1</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 11:29:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Hong Kong activist jailed for 10 more years for collusion with foreign forces</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-hong-kong-activist-jailed-for-10-more-years-for-collusion-with-foreign-forces</link><description>
Hong Kong democracy activist Joshua Wong was sentenced to 10 more years in jail on Thursday for colluding with foreign powers, the second time he has been penalised under the city's national security law. Hong, 30, is one of the most globally recognised faces of Hong Kong's pro-democracy movement and has already spent almost six years behind bars. He is now not due for release until late 2036. 
